(DocuMind Research Paper: Advances in Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Tj T*
(Author: AI Systems Lab \(September 2026\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Abstract:) Tj T*
(Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) significantly reduces factual hallucinations) Tj T*
(in large language models by grounding output in domain-specific corpus excerpts.) Tj T*
(In this work, we demonstrate that chunking with 700 characters and 120 character) Tj T*
(sliding-window overlap preserves semantic continuity across complex paragraphs.) Tj T*
(Experiments indicate an accuracy boost from 64.2% to 91.8% on factual benchmarks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Section 1: Architecture and Page Grounding) Tj T*
(Standard LLMs often suffer from catastrophic forgetting and temporal cutoff.) Tj T*
(By binding page numbers and chunk offsets directly to vector embeddings,) Tj T*
(the inference engine provides users with verifiable citations for all factual claims.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
